          "tool_name": "forensic_metascience__grim_percentage",
          "description": "Apply GRIM test to a percentage. More powerful than testing means directly. ONLY valid when the percentage is a SHARE of the sample -- 100*k/n for an integer count k of the n units. You MUST pass data_type: 'proportion'|'binary'|'count' when the percentage is such a share, or 'continuous' when it is a mean change, a concentration or a ratio (GRIM then refuses instead of manufacturing a false impossibility -- e.g. \"glucose fell 23.7%\"). Parameters: percentage (0-100), n (int), decimals (int, default 1), data_type (str, REQUIRED -- omitting it refuses rather than assuming a share)",
